Lane dh-join, 2026-10-12. Apply after root's restart puts default on 88e7651da or later
(`bin/seon check` runs the operator of default's running commit; before 88e7651da that operator keys
program classes without the test tree and loads a stale seon.test-support, so this slice cannot be proven).

Cause of the m3 "Datahike join" red: not Datahike. `seon.test-support/task-row` names the fixture symbol
by the bare hex handle; a handle leading with a digit (10 in 16) prints as `fixture.tasks/0f74...`, which
no reader accepts, so the hosted form refuses "Invalid symbol" and writes nothing, and
`seon.cluster.host-test/a-hosted-run-lands-on-its-branch-and-the-parent-head-is-unchanged` is red at random,
on HEAD as with m3's schema (bisect runs: HEAD red 2 of 3, HEAD+schema red 1 of 3). With a letter-leading handle
and m3's schema the join answers the receipt with and without the result cache and the planner (two runs).

Commit:
  git apply docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/dh-join-task-row.patch
  bin/lane commit LANE -m MSG --test seon.cluster.evaluate-source-test/code-evaluates-as-one-ordinary-run-of-its-agent \
    --test seon.cluster.host-test/a-hosted-run-lands-on-its-branch-and-the-parent-head-is-unchanged \
    test/seon/test_support.clj test/seon/cluster/evaluate_source_test.clj
Red on HEAD: the evaluate-source row (digit-leading handle) answers "Invalid symbol: fixture.tasks/0...".

